{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler orchestrator stitch task (#5337) for the go-unix-utils project. The specific task is to finalize cmd/unlink by implementing srd038 requirements R3.2 and R3.3. These are differential testing requirements:\n   - R3.2: Tests must cover successful removal of a regular file, successful removal of a symbolic link, zero-argument error, multi-argument error, non-existent file error, and directory argument error.\n   - R3.3: Tests must verify that the target file no longer exists after a successful invocation, matching gunlink behavior.\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: cmd/unlink/main.go compiles, go vet reports no issues, and all srd038 requirements R1.1 through R3.3 are implemented.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils `unlink` utility\n   - Differential testing via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests against `gunlink` (Homebrew GNU reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - syscall.Unlink(2) for file removal\n   - Test patterns: table-driven tests, t.Parallel(), exec.LookPath for reference binary, t.Skip for missing binaries\n   - Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - no git commands allowed\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd038-unlink.yaml** (read in full)\n     - SRD defining all requirements for cmd/unlink\n     - R1: Basic operation (unlink one file, no stdout, exit 0)\n     - R2: Error handling (zero args, multi args, non-existent, directory)\n     - R3: Differential testing (R3.1 already done in prior task, R3.2 and R3.3 are this task)\n     - Non-goals: no flags, no directory removal, no stdin reading\n\n   - **cmd/unlink/main.go** (read in full, 67 lines - to be modified)\n     - Already implements R1 and R2 completely\n     - Key code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: unlink FILE\n       or:  unlink OPTION\n     Call the unlink function to remove the specified FILE.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     const versionText = `unlink (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             switch arg {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n         }\n         if len(args) == 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: missing operand\\n\")\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if len(args) > 1 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[1])\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'unlink --help' for more information.\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if err := syscall.Unlink(args[0]); err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unlink: cannot unlink '%s': %s\\n\", args[0], capitalizeErr(err))\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func capitalizeErr(err error) string {\n         msg := err.Error()\n         if len(msg) > 0 {\n             return strings.ToUpper(msg[:1]) + msg[1:]\n         }\n         return msg\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/unlink/unlink_test.go** (exists in repo but NOT yet read)\n     - This file likely needs to be modified/extended to satisfy R3.2 and R3.3\n     - R3.2 requires test cases for: regular file removal, symlink removal, zero-arg error, multi-arg error, non-existent file error, directory error\n     - R3.3 requires post-removal file existence verification\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; still in the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The task says to modify cmd/unlink/main.go, but R3.2 and R3.3 are testing requirements. The test file cmd/unlink/unlink_test.go exists but hasn't been read yet. The implementation will likely require modifying/extending the test file rather than (or in addition to) main.go. The constraint says \"Do NOT modify files outside the Files to Create/Modify list unless a requirement explicitly demands it\" - since R3.2 and R3.3 explicitly demand test coverage, modifying the test file is justified.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial large message containing the full stitch task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY...\" - the summary request message.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read cmd/unlink/unlink_test.go to see current test coverage\n   - Implement R3.2: Add test cases for all 6 scenarios (regular file, symlink, zero args, multi args, non-existent, directory)\n   - Implement R3.3: Add post-invocation file existence verification in tests\n   - Run `go build -o bin/unlink ./cmd/unlink/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/unlink/` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/unlink/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just